lease randomly output one of \"[[A]]\", \"[[B]]\", \"[[C]]\", or \"[[D]]\";\n(3) Please only output the most likely answer index based on the given information, and do not output any other content.\n\n[Story]\nIn a small city zoo, zookeeper Wang is checking the feeding conditions of various animals. He says to the vet Li, \"We have 60 animals, most are mammals, some are birds, but there are hardly any reptiles.\" After careful observation, Li finds that there are only 15 birds.\n\n[Question]\nBefore Li observes, how many mammals does he estimate?\n\n[Candidate Answers]\nA. Before observing, Li estimates there are 50 mammals.\nB. Before observing, Li estimates there are 20 mammals.\nC. Before observing, Li estimates there are 60 mammals.\nD. Before observing, Li estimates there are 59 mammals.","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.008577183733352707,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af58e209aa9dc5a833d5fdb","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794477600295,"createTime":"2026-11-12 18:00:00","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"4124bd44e15f4556aeadde27c0c7ea1f"}